{
  "summary": "Corrects invalid OpenRPC default values emitted by `getopenrpcinfo`. Specifically, it changes `getdeploymentinfo.blockhash` to use a default hint instead of an invalid prose string as a literal default, and updates `send.options.include_watching` to default to boolean `false` rather than a string.",
  "problem": "Schema validators fail or encounter internal inconsistencies because `getopenrpcinfo` exports schema defaults that violate their declared types: `getdeploymentinfo` uses explanatory text as a fallback blockhash, and `send` uses a string default for a boolean parameter.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"`getopenrpcinfo` emits two defaults that do not satisfy their schemas.\"",
    "Commit 77c2a5c428: \"The fallback text describes how an omitted blockhash is resolved. It is not a valid hash and should not appear as a JSON Schema default. Emit it as a Bitcoin-specific hint so schema validators do not treat the prose as a permissible blockhash.\"",
    "Commit 87c7e00e08: \"The include_watching option is declared as boolean, but its string default makes the generated schema internally inconsistent.\"",
    "Milestoned for 32.0 and labeled 'Needs Backport (32.x)'."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "Small metadata and schema adjustment spanning RPC and wallet documentation (+10/-2 across 3 files).",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "This pull request fixes invalid OpenRPC defaults generated by the `getopenrpcinfo` RPC. Schema validators currently reject the output or hit inconsistencies because `getdeploymentinfo` uses a prose string as a default blockhash and `send.options.include_watching` specifies a string default for a boolean field. The change marks the prose blockhash as a hint and sets `include_watching` to boolean false. It is milestoned for 32.0 and marked for backport to 32.x.",
  "needs": [
    "diff"
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "uncertainties": [],
  "risk": {
    "level": "low",
    "touches": [
      "rpc_api"
    ],
    "why": "A mistake would only affect the schema documentation output in `getopenrpcinfo` without altering runtime RPC parameter handling or node operation."
  }
}
